And worst alike shall find and share:
The wicked cease from troubling there,
And there the weary are at rest;

ceaselessly:
My heart cried like a beaten child
Ceaselessly all night long;
I had to take my own cries

ceaseless:
Ere sleep comes down to soothe the weary eyes,
Which all the day with ceaseless care have sought
The magic gold which from the seeker flies;

ceas'd:
She, who late wish'd that Leonard might return,
Has ceas'd to languish, and forgot to mourn;
To the same high empyreal mansions come,

ceaseth:
Until the dawning of the day.'
But he said: 'The wind ceaseth, Maid;
Of chill nor damp be thou afraid.'
